  "id": "group-experiment",
  "term": "group experiment",
  "definition": "A group experiment is a research design in which participants are divided into separate groups so each group receives a different condition or combination of conditions, often alongside a control group. The groups are then compared on the same assessments to examine the effects of the different interventions.",
